            <ArticleTitle>[18F]ODIBO: a prosthetic group for bioorthogonal radiolabeling of macromolecules via strain-promoted alkyne-azide cycloaddition.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02532g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel prosthetic group for the efficient radiolabeling of macromolecules has been developed. [18F]oxadibenzocyclooctyne ([18F]ODIBO) is synthesized in high radiochemical yield and applied for nearly quantitative conjugation to azide-tagged peptides and proteins at room temperature and low substrate concentrations. The resulting bioconjugates are chemically and radiochemically pure and free of toxic solvents and catalysts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
